-- title:
--   Affine node chart at an Igusa–Drinfeld crossing
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $5\le q$ and a non-zero natural number $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}=\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\,\mathbb Q$ which lies over $q$, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$ (`LiesOverPrime`). Throughout, a place of a field extension $F/K$ is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, different from $F$ and a principal ideal ring, $P.\mathrm{ord}$ denotes the associated normalised valuation, and $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$ the residue evaluation, taken in $K$ when the place is rational.
--
--   The following data are given. A finite set $W$ of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ — that field being the subfield of the Laurent series over the residue field of $A$ generated by the $q$-expansions $j$ and $j(M'\cdot)$ — and the hypothesis `hW` that $W$ consists exactly of the supersingular places, i.e. of those $w$ which are rational, which are affine geometric places, and for which $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the geometric $j$-generator lies in the supersingular $j$-set of $q$. An inclusion `hle` of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ (the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full modular function field of level $M'$, inside Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) into $\overline F:=\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ (the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the function field of the level-$(q^2M',\;\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M')$ curve). A constant reduction $R_0$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ over $A$ with values in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$: that is, a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, a residue homomorphism onto the reduction field with kernel the maximal ideal, a map on places preserving degrees and compatible with divisor push-forward, the condition that a constant lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ exactly when it lies in $A$ with the expected residue, and the property that every non-zero element can be scaled by a constant so as to have non-zero residue. The hypothesis `hR₀` states that $R_0$ computes coefficientwise reduction: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose image in Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, that image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Further, an element $\pi\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$ and $\pi\in A$; an index $\zeta\in\mathrm{Idx}\,q$, i.e. a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; and two families of valuation subrings of $\overline F$, namely $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ indexed by $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)=\mathrm{CuspidalType.ProjLine}\,q$ and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ indexed by $W$.
--
--   The Igusa hypotheses are: `hIg_inf`, which describes $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ as the set of $f\in\overline F$ for which there are Laurent series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ having non-zero coefficientwise reduction and $f\cdot y=x$ in Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; `hIg`, which asserts that every $\ell$ is obtained from $\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q$ by some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')\subseteq SL(2,\mathbb Z)$ whose reduction $\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma$ carries $\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q$ to $\ell$, with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the preimage of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ under $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$; `hIg_inj`, the injectivity of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$; and `hIg_perm`, which asserts that for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ the preimages of the $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ under $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ are again the members of the family, permuted by some permutation of $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$.
--
--   The supersingular hypotheses are: `hSS_A`, that for each $s\in W$ and $x\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$ the image of $x$ in $\overline F$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ exactly when $x\in A$; `hSS_over`, which for $s\in W$ and $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ such that $f$ has no pole at any place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which $\hat j$ has no pole (here $\hat j$ denotes the image of the $q$-expansion $jq$ under coefficientwise embedding, viewed in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$), and such that the $R_0$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$, asserts that the image of $f$ in $\overline F$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$, and that for every $a\in A$ whose residue in $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue, the difference of the image of $f$ and the image of $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$; `hSS_fix`, that each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is stable under pullback along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; and `hSS_tr`, that for each $s$ there is $t\in O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ such that for every $a\in A$ the difference $t-a$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and is a unit there.
--
--   The descent data are: a subfield $K_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ algebraic over $K_0$ and $\pi\in K_0$; a commutative domain $A_0$ which is a discrete valuation ring and a Henselian local ring, together with an injective local homomorphism $\iota:A_0\to A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is exactly $A\cap K_0$ (`hιK₀`), such that the composite of $\iota$ with the residue map of $A$ is surjective (`hres`); a generator $\varpi_0$ of the maximal ideal of $A_0$ (`hϖ₀`) with $\iota(\varpi_0)=\pi$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (`hϖ₀π`); a subfield $F_0\subseteq\overline F$ characterised by `hF₀` as consisting of those elements all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in $K_0$; the hypothesis `hjF₀` that the image of $\hat j$ in $\overline F$ lies in $F_0$; and an $A_0$-algebra structure on $F_0$ pinned by `hj₀` to $\iota$, i.e. $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,A_0\,F_0$ sends $a$ to the image of $\iota(a)$ under $\overline{\mathbb Q}\to\overline F$.
--
--   The model data are: a scheme $X_0$ and a morphism $\mathrm{toBase}_0:X_0\to\operatorname{Spec}A_0$ with $X_0$ integral and $\mathrm{toBase}_0$ proper, flat and locally of finite presentation; the normality hypothesis `hn₀` that every stalk of $X_0$ is integrally closed; a ring isomorphism $\varphi_0:F_0\to\mathcal K(X_0)$ identifying $F_0$ with the function field, compatible by `hφ₀` with the constants, i.e. $\varphi_0(\mathrm{algebraMap}\,A_0\,F_0\,a)=\mathrm{baseToFunctionField}\,\mathrm{toBase}_0\,a$, the germ at the generic point of the global section pulled back from $a$; and the relative-dimension-one hypothesis `hdim`: for all $\eta,y\in X_0$, if $\eta$ lies over the closed point of $A_0$, if $\eta$ specialises to some point distinct from $\eta$, and if $\eta\rightsquigarrow y$ with $y\neq\eta$, then $y$ is closed, i.e. every $z$ with $y\rightsquigarrow z$ equals $y$. For $x\in X_0$, $\mathrm{localRing}\,X_0\,\varphi_0\,x$ denotes the subring of $F_0$ obtained by transporting the image of the stalk at $x$ in the function field back along $\varphi_0$. The component dictionary is a map $\mathrm{gen}:\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)\sqcup W\to X_0$ satisfying: `hgenIg`, that $f\in\mathrm{localRing}\,X_0\,\varphi_0\,(\mathrm{gen}(\mathrm{inl}\,\ell))$ exactly when $f$, read in $\overline F$, lies in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$; `hgenSS`, the same with $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ for the points $\mathrm{gen}(\mathrm{inr}\,s)$; `hgen₀`, that every $\mathrm{gen}\,i$ lies over the closed point of $A_0$; and `hgen`, that a point $x$ over the closed point is of the form $\mathrm{gen}\,i$ exactly when it is not closed, i.e. exactly when it specialises to some $y\neq x$.
--
--   Finally, let $\ell\in\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ and $s\in W$ be given.
--
--   The conclusion asserts the existence of an $A_0$-subalgebra $B\subseteq F_0$, a maximal ideal $\mathfrak m$ of $B$, and a point $x_0\in X_0$ with the following properties.
--
--   1. $B$ is a finitely generated $A_0$-algebra.
--
--   2. The ring $\mathrm{localRing}\,X_0\,\varphi_0\,x_0$ is integrally closed in $F_0$: every $x\in F_0$ integral over it belongs to it.
--
--   3. $F_0$ is the field of fractions of $B$: every $x\in F_0$ admits $b,c\in B$ with $c\neq 0$ and $x\,c=b$.
--
--   4. Every prime ideal $\mathfrak q$ of $B$ which contains the ideal generated by the image of the maximal ideal of $A_0$ and which is not maximal is a minimal prime over that ideal.
--
--   5. For every $\eta\in X_0$ lying over the closed point of $A_0$ which is not closed (it specialises to some point distinct from itself), if $B\subseteq\mathrm{localRing}\,X_0\,\varphi_0\,\eta$ then there is a prime $\mathfrak q$ of $B$ such that $\mathrm{localRing}\,X_0\,\varphi_0\,\eta$ is the localisation of $B$ at $\mathfrak q$, in the sense that $x$ lies in it exactly when $x\,c=b$ for some $b,c\in B$ with $c\notin\mathfrak q$.
--
--   6. Conversely, for every minimal prime $\mathfrak q$ over the ideal generated by the image of the maximal ideal of $A_0$ there is a non-closed point $\eta\in X_0$ over the closed point of $A_0$ whose local ring is the localisation of $B$ at $\mathfrak q$ in the same sense.
--
--   7. The element $\hat j$ of $F_0$ provided by `hjF₀` lies in $B$.
--
--   8. The image of $\varpi_0$ in $B$ lies in $\mathfrak m$.
--
--   9. The point $x_0$ lies over the closed point of $A_0$ and is closed: every $y$ with $x_0\rightsquigarrow y$ equals $x_0$.
--
--   10. $\mathrm{localRing}\,X_0\,\varphi_0\,x_0$ is the localisation of $B$ at $\mathfrak m$: $f\in F_0$ lies in it exactly when $f\,c=b$ for some $b,c\in B$ with $c\notin\mathfrak m$.
--
--   11. For every index $i$, $\mathrm{gen}\,i\rightsquigarrow x_0$ holds exactly when $i=\mathrm{inl}\,\ell$ or $i=\mathrm{inr}\,s$.
--
--   12. $\mathrm{gen}(\mathrm{inl}\,\ell)\neq\mathrm{gen}(\mathrm{inr}\,s)$.
--
--   13. The structure homomorphism $A_0\to B_{\mathfrak m}$ to the localisation at $\mathfrak m$ is not formally smooth.
--
--   14. The stalk of $X_0$ at $x_0$ is a Noetherian ring, and there is a natural number $w\ge 1$ such that $w$ is a unit in $A_0$ together with a ring isomorphism
--   $$e:\widehat{\mathcal O_{X_0,x_0}}\;\longrightarrow\;\widehat{A_0}[[u,v]]/\bigl(uv-\varpi_0^{\,w}\bigr),$$
--   where the left-hand side is the adic completion of the stalk at $x_0$ with respect to its maximal ideal, the right-hand side is the ring of formal power series in two variables $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,2)$ over the adic completion $\widehat{A_0}$ of $A_0$ at its maximal ideal, modulo the principal ideal generated by $X_0X_1-C(\varpi_0^{\,w})$, and such that $e$ is compatible with the base: for every $a\in A_0$, $e$ sends the image in the completion of the germ at $x_0$ of the global section of $X_0$ pulled back from $a$ along $\mathrm{toBase}_0$ to the class of the constant power series with value the image of $a$ in $\widehat{A_0}$.
--
--   This is the node chart of the descended full-level modular curve: an affine normal $A_0$-chart of the model $X_0$ around the closed point at which the Igusa component indexed by $\ell$ meets the supersingular (Drinfeld) component indexed by $s$, exhibiting that point as lying on exactly those two components, as not formally smooth over the base, and as having completed local ring the crossing $\widehat{A_0}[[u,v]]/(uv-\varpi_0^{w})$ with $w$ prime to the residue characteristic. It feeds the corresponding Igusa and Drinfeld chart statements and the construction of the semistable scheme over the descent base.
